    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JAPAN\nKimontin\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktaitio\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nApéritif\nCocktail tidbits\nHors d'Oeuvre Gastronomiques\nSelected gourmet delicacies\nRôti au Vol\nA selected cut of aged beef, turkey or other succulent meat\nroasted on board and caved to order\nYour flight attendant will advise you of today's roast\nSuprême de Volaille Wellington\nBoneless breast of chicken baked in puff pastry\nBlanquette de Veau\nTender morsels of veal simmered with cream and mushrooms.\nFilet de Sole Meunière\nSole fillets sautéed in butter with lemon juice and parsley\nPlat du Jour\nSpecialty of the day\nPommes de Terre Maison\nPotatoes Maison\nRiz Pilaf\nRice Pilaf",
      "Filet de Sole Meunière\nSole fillets sautéed in butter with lemon juice and parsley\nPlat du Jour\nSpecialty of the day\nPommes de Terre Maison\nPotatoes Maison\nRiz Pilaf\nRice Pilaf\nLégumes au Beurre\nButtered vegetable bouquet\nSalade Campagnarde\nTossed garden salad\nSélection de Fruits et Fromages\nSelection of fruits and cheeses\nDessert\nDessert\nCafé\nCoffee\nThé\nTea\nCafé Décaféiné\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di Saronno Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nCointreau\n189 K005(J)",
      "JAPAN\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and paintina\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\nJAPAN is a land of contrasts. It can display the most neon-lit, skyscrapered and expressway-lined\nface, yet finds its inspiration in the quiet beauty of the graceful Tori Gate and Mt. Fuji, pictured here\nThe Japanese can run their trains at lightening speed, vet spend hours on a small conversational\ncourtesy. Here you will find graceful perfection and formality contrasted with vigorous commerce\nAmong the many stylish hotels in the capital city of Tokyo is the Keio Plaza Inter-Continental\nPan Am serves Tokyo on its Round-The-World flights and nonstop daily from New York, San Francisco\nLos Angeles, Honolulu, and Hong Kong. Osaka is served nonstop from Honolulu\n1993:01,095\nOPAN AM."
    ],
